Branch-per-feature, the branch may live for a week before it merges

Definition of “DONE”:
    Feature is implemented
    Code follows the project’s coding standards
    Unit tests have been written
    All excision tests pass
    Feature has been manually tested
    No known critical bugs remain
    Documentation has been updated if necessary
    Code has been reviewed and approved
    Changes have been merged into main

Sprint Length = 2 weeks
    Sprint Planning - Every 2 weeks to decide what work will be done
    Meeting - 2 times per week to share progress/roadblocks
    Review - Every 2 weeks to share completed work
    Opinion - Every 2 weeks to share what went well/wrong
    Backlog refinement - Once per week to prepare upcoming tasks

Pull Requests:
-> Developer
-> Create feature branch
-> Write Code + Tests
-> Create Pull Requests
-> Code Review
-> Approved
-> Merge into main

Pull Request Rules:
    Every change must be submitted through a pull request
    The author may not approve their own PR unless reviewed by another team member
    At least 1 other team member must approve a PR
    All automated tests must pass before merging
    Requested changes must be addressed before merging
    If a review has no response for 24-48 hours, the author should either remind the reviewer or ask another team member to review it

What the reviewer should check:
    Does the code solve the intended problem?
    Is the code readable?
    Are there appropriate tests?
    Could the change break existing functionality?
    Does it follow the project’s coding standards?